Reaffirming its strong commitment to the unity, sovereignty, independence, and territorial integrity of Yemen,

Expressing grave concern at the continued conflict and instability in Yemen, reaffirming the obligation of all parties to comply with international humanitarian law and international human rights law as applicable, and expressing alarm at the significant ongoing humanitarian challenges faced by the civilian population, including obstacles to full, safe, and unhindered humanitarian access,

Reaffirming its strong support for the efforts of the Special Envoy of the Secretary-General for Yemen to advance an inclusive, Yemeni-led and Yemeni-owned political process under United Nations auspices, and emphasizing that there is no military solution to the conflict,

Expressing serious concern at the ongoing detention by the Houthis of United Nations personnel, personnel of international and non-governmental organisations, and diplomatic personnel, and demanding their immediate, safe, and unconditional release,

Reaffirming the importance of maritime security, the safety of seafarers, and navigational rights and freedoms of commercial and merchant vessels in the Red Sea and Gulf of Aden in accordance with international law, demanding an immediate cessation of attacks on merchant and commercial vessels, and expressing grave concern at the illicit transfer of weapons and military materiel into Yemen in violation of the targeted arms embargo established pursuant to resolution 2216 (2015),

