2. Emphasises the importance of facilitating humanitarian assistance and commercial imports of essential goods to meet civilians’ basic survival needs, reaffirms its decision in resolution 2664 (2022), and calls upon all parties to refrain from actions that exacerbate the economic and humanitarian hardships faced by the Yemeni people;

3. Decides to extend until 15 December 2026 the mandate of the Panel of Experts as contained in paragraph 21 of resolution 2140 (2014) and paragraph 21 of resolution 2216 (2015), and expresses its intention to review the mandate and take appropriate action regarding the further extension no later than 15 November 2026;

